# Tattletale HUD baseline: rows you already know are benign, labelled "known" in the HUD.
# Copy to tattletale.hud-baseline at the repository root (git-ignored), or pass
# --hud-baseline PATH. Only the HUD reads it; the watchers ignore it and nothing is hidden.
#
# One pattern per line, matched against the text of a row (for an alert: "KIND message"):
#   plain text      a case-sensitive substring
#   re:REGEX        a Python regular expression, searched anywhere in the row
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Leading and trailing spaces are trimmed.
#
# These entries are generic examples; replace them with what you see on your own machine.

# A test runner's JVM that listens on all interfaces while tests run.
re:^LISTEN! EXPOSED on all interfaces java pid \d+

# Your own git asking the macOS keychain for a credential.
git-credential-osxkeychain

# Programs signed by Apple.
re:\| signer: Software Signing team:
